From 269131da6b47522a058d5777a6e2b47e0855ed49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bare <git@barebrowser.org>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 23:02:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Say which autofill service is filling, without naming Google

Payment methods and Addresses and more both opened on a card headed "Google
isn't your autofill provider", with the G mark beside it and a body offering to
use payment info from a Google Account.

The card itself is right and should stay. It appears when
getAndroidAutofillFrameworkAvailability reports AVAILABLE, which means a
non-Google Android autofill service is selected and usable, and it explains why
the toggles beneath it are greyed out. Its button opens the Autofill services
screen, which patch 0046 already renamed. Google's own provider reports
ANDROID_AUTOFILL_SERVICE_IS_GOOGLE instead, so the card never described this
build accurately: the service doing the filling here is whatever the user chose
in Android, and the alternative is Autofill with Bare rather than a Google
Account.

So the wording says that instead, and the icon is the neutral ic_info_24dp that
the extensions menu and Safety check already use, rather than a new asset.

The condition is untouched. The same availability call decides WebauthnMode in
ChromeAuthenticatorFactory, where AVAILABLE means CHROME_3PP_ENABLED, so
narrowing it to quiet a string would have moved passkeys off the chosen
provider. Nothing here reaches autofill behaviour, provider selection,
Credential Manager or WebAuthn.

Settings search needs no separate change. AutofillPaymentMethodsFragment adds
the card to the index by string id under the same condition, so the search
result reads the new wording too.
